---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About"
	description="Yeh Bro is an Australia-first bodybuilding brand — PED culture education with harm reduction, evidence-first lifting, and legal sports nutrition only. We never sell gear."
>
	<article class="prose-wrap">
		<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
		<h1>AU lifters. Real PED talk. Legal nutrition.</h1>
		<p class="lede">
			Yeh Bro is an Australia-first bodybuilding and lifting brand. We educate hard on PED and
			bodybuilding culture — risks, bloodwork, legality, coming off — and we monetise legal sports
			nutrition only. Not a gear shop. Not a clinic.
		</p>

		<h2>Who we are</h2>
		<p>
			We publish for people who train hard and want straight answers: how gym culture actually works,
			what PEDs mean in that culture, and what belongs in a legal stack (creatine, protein, pre,
			basics). Ignoring pharmacology in bodybuilding creates naivety. Selling grey gear helps the
			wrong people. We do neither.
		</p>

		<h2>PED education = harm reduction</h2>
		<p>
			When PED reality comes up, the frame is <strong>education and harm reduction</strong> — not
			moral panic and not a storefront:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Health risks at a population level — cardiovascular, endocrine, hepatic, injection/quality unknowns</li>
			<li>Australian legal context at a high level — possession, supply, and import can be illegal or restricted; we are not your lawyer</li>
			<li>Bloodwork and medical supervision as clinical care — not DIY protocols from a fitness site</li>
			<li>Mental health and coming off under a qualified clinician — not a PCT product funnel</li>
			<li>Legal sports nutrition stays general training / wellness — never “on-cycle” or “blast” shop framing</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Start with
			<a href="/blog/ped-harm-reduction-australia">PED harm reduction (AU)</a>
			and
			<a href="/blog/bodybuilding-culture-education">bodybuilding culture education</a>.
			Nothing here is medical advice, diagnosis, or a green light to break the law.
		</p>

		<h2>How we pick products we link</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Evidence and clear labels over marketing copy</li>
			<li>Dose you can verify — proprietary blends are a red flag</li>
			<li>AU availability and price per effective dose</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Affiliate / product recommendations:</strong> legal sports nutrition only (creatine,
				protein, pre/intra, basics) — never cycle / blast / PCT shopping lists
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>We are not pay-to-rank. Sponsored posts, if any, get labelled separately.</p>

		<h2>What we never do</h2>
		<div class="skip-flag">
			<p>
				We do <strong>not</strong> sell, source, or promote buying illegal AAS, restricted SARMs,
				unapproved peptides, underground lab gear, or grey-market “buy gear” / cycle-blast-PCT product
				funnels. We do not publish personal dosing protocols that replace a doctor. Comment bait
				asking for sources gets refused. Education ≠ a storefront.
			</p>
		</div>

		<h2>Affiliate relationships</h2>
		<p>
			Some links use <code>/go/</code> redirects. If you buy, we may earn a commission at no extra
			cost to you. Full policy on <a href="/disclosure">Disclosure</a>.
		</p>

		<div class="cta-row">
			<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/blog/ped-harm-reduction-australia">PED education</a>
			<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/start-here">Start here</a>
		</div>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
